-- title:
--   Correction coordinates, the concrete cylinder bases and the concrete space
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to the construction of a separable Banach space $Z$ that contains no linear copy of $c_0$, yet $Z\times c_0$ is bi-Lipschitz equivalent to $Z$ and $Z$ is Lipschitz-universal for separable metric spaces. $Z$ is a completion of the space of molecules on the unit ball of $c_0$ (finitely supported functions with total sum zero), normed by test functions from carefully chosen Lipschitz classes. Levels are pairs $(i,n)$, labels are (level, band, grid tag), and the coordinates of $c_0$ are split into row coordinates indexed by $\mathbb N$ and label coordinates indexed by labels.
--
--   1. **Correction coordinates.** For a level they are the prefix $\{0,\dots,J-1\}$, the row coordinate of $i$, and the radius coordinates of the level and of the previous level. The correction of a label depends only on these coordinates.
--   2. **Base functions.** The correction base of a label $\gamma$ is its correction, viewed as a function on the cube of correction coordinates. It is bounded by $4$ and $(4+12\eta)$-Lipschitz.
--   3. **Concrete bases.** These base functions, with the bands of the labels and the band lengths $\ell_j$, form a family of cylinder bases.
--   4. **Localizations.** Tags extended by zero give a tag localization: the prefix of every point in the support lies within $2\cdot2^{-j}$ of the tag. The terminal labels (band $=J$) and the minimal radius coordinate give a radius localization.
--   5. **The space.** The concrete space is
--   $$
--   Z=\overline{\bigl(\mathrm{Mol}(B),\|\cdot\|_{\mathrm{sel}}\bigr)}
--   $$
--   for the source classes generated by these bases.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/C0Absorption/Tags.lean

